      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence consistently states the dataset (SESAME) is automatically generated without human supervision. The Abstract says the authors 'propose a method to automatically generate labeled datasets for NER from public data sources.' The Introduction states they 'propose a method to construct labeled datasets without human supervision for NER' and describes it as a 'weakly-supervised dataset (i.e. a silver standard corpora),' noting 'The methodology to automatically generate our dataset...' The SESAME section confirms they 'create a massive silver standard dataset for NER' and only exclude sentences lacking annotated entities. Thus the evidence supports that the dataset generation is fully automated (silver standard, no human annotation), so the answer is yes."
      },
